NAME
    window - Generalized Terminal Session Launcher

SYNOPSIS
    window [OPTIONS] [sudo] COMMAND [ARGS]...

DESCRIPTION
    window is a wrapper utility that executes any given command or program 
    in a newly spawned gnome-terminal instance. It safely handles privilege 
    escalation (sudo) and allows you to detach long-running processes or 
    editors from your current terminal session.

    If no window-sizing options are passed, window will read the default 
    behavior from the configuration file located at /etc/window/settings.conf.

OPTIONS
    -f, --full-screen
        Opens the new gnome-terminal in full-screen mode.

    -m, --maximize
        Opens the new gnome-terminal in a maximized window.

    -n, --normal
        Opens the new gnome-terminal using the default window size.

    -h, --help
        Displays this help text and exits.

SPECIAL KEYWORDS
    sudo
        If 'sudo' is included before the command, window will prompt 
        for your password in the new terminal window and execute the 
        subsequent command with root privileges.

EXAMPLES
    window htop
        Opens the htop system monitor in a new window using the default 
        view from settings.conf.

    window -m dotnet run
        Spawns a maximized terminal window and executes a C# .NET 
        application, keeping your main terminal free for other tasks.

    window -f sudo nano /etc/hosts /etc/fstab
        Opens both /etc/hosts and /etc/fstab using nano in a new, 
        full-screen terminal with root privileges.

    window npm start
        Starts a React development server in a detached, standard-sized 
        terminal window.

FILES
    /etc/window/settings.conf
        Configuration file. Use DEFAULT_VIEW to set base behavior 
        (e.g., DEFAULT_VIEW=-f).
        
    /etc/window/help
        This documentation file.
